NV_PK(38,{"beitou library is taiwan's first green library it is built with lots of wood":"","the library is in beitou park part of its roof makes power from sunlight and it saves rainwater for its toilets":"","this is beitou park on the left you can see the roof of beitou library":"","beitou hot spring museum was built in 1913 as a public bathhouse when japan ruled taiwan":"","the big bath is on the first floor with roman arches and columns all around":"","stained glass windows light up the bath they were rare and costly back then":"","upstairs on the second floor there is a big tatami room":"","this museum panel shows beitou's three main kinds of hot spring water":"","thermal valley has a green sulfur spring white steam rises from the hot water":"","the water can reach about 90 degrees celsius and is strongly acidic stay behind the railing":"","which hot spring is green tap one":"","yes thermal valley has the green sulfur spring":"","not this one look at the photos again":""});